  "worked_solution": "We substitute $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\u27e86\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,{sin}^{2}\u2061(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}),\\,{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83,\\,\\frac{3}{4}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
